IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ga-dates`
IMPORT `ga-treatment`

-- Guardianship Act 1987 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in ga-treatment.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases -- medical and dental treatment`

`d` MEANS `the date`

`not treatment` MEANS `not medical or dental treatment for Part 5`
`trial` MEANS `treatment in the course of a clinical trial`
`special` MEANS `special treatment`
`major` MEANS `major treatment`
`minor` MEANS `minor treatment`

`PR` MEANS `my person responsible gave it`
`G` MEANS `my guardian gave it`
`T` MEANS `the Tribunal gave it`

`adult` MEANS `d` 1 1 1940
`treatment day` MEANS `d` 1 6 2026

§§ `ss 33(2), 34 -- does Part 5 apply`

-- Arguments: date of birth; day of treatment; can understand; can indicate. 16 on the day, and one day short.
#ASSERT `Does Part 5 apply to me` (`d` 1 7 2010) (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does Part 5 apply to me` (`d` 1 7 2010) (`d` 1 7 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does Part 5 apply to me` (`d` 2 7 2010) (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does Part 5 apply to me` `adult` `treatment day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does Part 5 apply to me` `adult` `treatment day` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 33(1) -- the kind of treatment`

-- Arguments: treatment; non-intrusive diagnostic; first aid; non-prescription drug; declared not treatment; clinical
-- trial; sterilising; new; declared special; declared major.
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `minor`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `major`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `special`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `special`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `special`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `trial`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not treatment`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not treatment`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not treatment`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not treatment`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not treatment`
#ASSERT `What kind of treatment is this` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not treatment`

§§ `s 33A -- my person responsible`

-- Arguments: date of birth; day; in care as a child; in the Secretary's care under s 13; guardian; guardian declined;
-- spouse; spouse declined; carer; carer declined; close friend or relative; friend declined.
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my guardian`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my spouse`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the person who has the care of me`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my close friend or relative`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no one`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no one`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my close friend or relative`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` `adult` `treatment day` `neither's care` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Secretary`
-- A child of 17 (s 33A(2)), and a person who turns 18 on the day.
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` (`d` 1 1 2009) `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the person with parental responsibility for me`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` (`d` 1 1 2009) `treatment day` `the Minister's care` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Minister`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` (`d` 1 1 2009) `treatment day` `the Secretary's care` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Secretary`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` (`d` 1 6 2008) `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `my guardian`
#ASSERT `Who is my person responsible` (`d` 2 6 2008) `treatment day` `neither's care` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the person with parental responsibility for me`

§§ `ss 36, 45A, 45AB -- who can consent`

-- Arguments: kind; have a person responsible; guardian's s 45A authority; Tribunal's s 45AB(1)(a) determination.
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `not treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 5 does not require consent to this`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `special` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `special` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Tribunal, or my guardian under the Tribunal's authority`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `trial` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my person responsible or the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `trial` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `only the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `trial` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `major` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my person responsible or the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `minor` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my person responsible or the Tribunal`
#ASSERT `Who can consent to my treatment` `minor` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only the Tribunal, as I have no person responsible`

§§ `s 37 -- without consent`

-- Arguments: kind; urgency; a person responsible can be contacted and will decide; s 37(3) certificate.
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `major` `to save my life` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `special` `to prevent serious damage to my health` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `special` `to prevent significant pain or distress` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `major` `to prevent significant pain or distress` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `trial` `to save my life` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `minor` `it is not urgent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `minor` `it is not urgent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `minor` `it is not urgent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `major` `it is not urgent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be treated without consent` `not treatment` `to save my life` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

